{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_email_bridge_imap_smtp", "label": "Email bridge, IMAP + SMTP (page)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/email-bridge.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_emailbridgeactor", "label": "EmailBridgeActor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/email-bridge.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The ops/alerting bridge otherwise hand-rolled in every project: a mailbox becomes a message source, SMTP a sink. Either half alone is valid; configuring neither, or an imap half without a target, is rejected at startup because both connect successfully and then do nothing."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_emailbridgeoptions", "label": "EmailBridgeOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/email-bridge.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Options merge one level deep, so supplying the imap or smtp group in code replaces the configured group wholesale rather than overriding single fields."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_at_least_once_settled_by_imap_flags", "label": "At-least-once, settled by IMAP flags", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/email-bridge.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "There is no in-memory bookkeeping: processed is a fact on the server, which is why a crashed consumer sees the message again rather than losing it."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_onprocessed_modes", "label": "onProcessed modes: markSeen and move", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/email-bridge.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "markSeen needs a dedicated mailbox, because anything marking mail read behind the bridge makes it skip messages; move must differ from the watched mailbox, since moving mail into the mailbox it is swept from redelivers it forever while every individual IMAP command in that loop succeeds."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_idle_polling_reconnection", "label": "IDLE, polling and reconnection", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/email-bridge.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A server without IDLE is polled on the same interval, which is a fully working mode rather than a degraded one; pollIntervalMs also bounds how long a refused message waits before redelivery, and imapflow reconnects not at all, so the BrokerActor lifecycle owns backoff, jitter and the breaker."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_one_actor_one_mailbox", "label": "One actor, one mailbox", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/email-bridge.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An IMAP connection can IDLE only on the mailbox it has selected, so a bridge watches exactly one and watching two means spawning two actors."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_pooled_smtp_outbound", "label": "Pooled SMTP outbound", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/email-bridge.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A server-rejected message is dropped with an error log rather than retried, because re-queueing parks the poisoned message at the head of the buffer and tears down a healthy pool; connection-level failures do the opposite and re-queue."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_emailtemplate", "label": "EmailTemplate", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/email-bridge.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Values are HTML-escaped by default with the SafeHtml brand as the one opt-out; setValue on an undeclared name and render with any placeholder unset both throw, because otherwise the failure only surfaces in a mail that has already been sent. It is deliberately logic-less, so a repeated fragment is built with html and passed in."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_email_bridge_imap_smtp", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_emailbridgeactor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/email-bridge.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_emailbridgeactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_emailbridgeoptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/email-bridge.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_emailbridgeactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_at_least_once_settled_by_imap_flags", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/email-bridge.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_at_least_once_settled_by_imap_flags", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_onprocessed_modes", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/email-bridge.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_emailbridgeactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_idle_polling_reconnection", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/email-bridge.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_emailbridgeactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_pooled_smtp_outbound", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/email-bridge.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_emailbridgeactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_emailtemplate", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/email-bridge.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_one_actor_one_mailbox", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_idle_polling_reconnection", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/email-bridge.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_emailbridgeactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_broker_actor_base_brokeractor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/email-bridge.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_idle_polling_reconnection", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_broker_actor_base_reconnect_with_backoff", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/email-bridge.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_email_bridge_pooled_smtp_outbound", "target": "docs_src_conten